Covers:
- How to deploy Windows and Linux EC2 instances using console, CLI and Powershell
- Remotely manage windows instances using RDP and linux instances using ssh
- Manage EC2 instance hibernation mode followed by monitoring instance performance

### Deploying Linux instance
Using
console:
CLI:
- aws ec2 run-instances --image-id <ami-id> --count 1 --instance-type t2.micro --key-name KeyPair1 --security-group-ids <sg-id> --subnet-id <subnet-id>
- aws ec2 create-tags --resources <instance-id> --tags Key=Name,Value=Linux2
Powershell:
- get-module -list *aws* : returns powershell module if avialable
- set-awscredential -accesskey $accesskey -secretkey $secretkey -storeas admin
- get-awscredential -listprofiledetail : returns existing aws credentials
- initialize-awsdefaultconfiguration -profilename admin1 : initializes AWS session with given credential/profile
- New-EC2Instance -ImageId <image-id> -MinCount 1 -MaxCount 1 -KeyName KeyPair1 -SecurityGroupId <sg-id> -InstanceType m1.small -SubnetId <subnet-id>
- get-ec2instance
- (get-ec2instance).instances
- (get-ec2instance).instances | get-member -type property : to list available properties 
- (get-ec2instance).instances.tags
- New-EC2Tag -ResourceId <instance-id> -Tag @{Key="Name",Value="Linux3"}

