### Managing EC2 instance Hibernation using console, CLI and Powershell
- When you hibernate a machine, the current state of operating system is saved to hibernation file. When you resume from hibernation mode, you are exactly where you left off.
- you have to enable/disable hibernation mode on EC2 instances while creating/launching them. you cannot do it on the already created/existed ones
- to launch an instance in hibernation mode, we need to encrypt root volume on device.
CLI:
- aws ec2 stop-instances --instance-ids <instance-id> --hibernate $true
Powershell:
- Stop-EC2Instance -InstanceId <instance-id> -Hibernate $true
